== The three new tests (v1 -> v2) ==
EnclosureTests.test_void_interval_replays_its_outward_log_exp_composition   kills M03a: replays endpoint(m) = _outward(-n*log_bounds(1-m, bits=BITS)) and asserts void_interval(mass, n) == (exp_neg_bounds(xhi(mass[1]))[0], exp_neg_bounds(xlo(mass[0]))[1]); fixtures mass=(1/7,1/5) n=4; mass=(1/(7*4**8),1/(5*4**8)) n=4**8 (n*m in (1/7,1/5); (1/7,1/5) itself at 4**8 raises 'Void exponential domain exhausted'); point mass (1/3,1/3) n=4; sanity lo < (1-m_hi)^n <= (1-m_lo)^n < hi on all three (holds on pristine and on the mutant, which is why containment alone could not kill it)
EnclosureTests.test_poisson_target_replays_its_outward_exp_composition      kills M03b: poisson_target(b) == (exp_neg_bounds(b[1])[0], exp_neg_bounds(b[0])[1]) for b = coefficient_interval() and b = (1/3,1/2); lo < hi; default argument equals the explicit coefficient interval
PredicateFixtureTests.test_overall_requires_every_status_to_pass           kills M21: _overall(['PASS','NOT_A_DECLARED_STATUS']) and _overall(['NOT_RUN','PASS','PASS']) are INCONCLUSIVE_PRECISION, _overall(['PASS','PASS']) is PASS, _overall([]) is INCONCLUSIVE_PRECISION

